/*--------------------------------------------
 Le Grand full theoretical eye: ACCOMMODATED (7.053 D)

 Source: TEVOI (Smith & Atchison, The Eye and Visual Optical Instruments, Cambridge University Press 1997), Appendix 3 'Schematic eyes', p. 785, Le Grand full theoretical eye: Accommodated.
 Surfaces 1-4: R 7.8, 6.5, 6.0, -5.5 mm; n 1.3771, 1.3374, 1.4270, 1.3360; d 0.55, 2.65, 4.5 mm. Eye power 67.677 D, length 24.197 mm.
 The cornea, aqueous and vitreous are as the relaxed eye; the lens is thicker and steeper and moves forward.
 Radii, thicknesses and indices are as published; nothing has been added (no retina is drawn: the appendix gives the eye length, 24.197 mm, not a retinal surface). The 4 mm stop is the app's usual pupil.
----------------------------------------------*/
